    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Kyle Tucker**, whose score of 66.85 establishes him as our definitive offensive anchor. Facing a favorable matchup against Landen Roupp (xERA 4.07), **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-floor profile that remains insulated from the volatility surrounding the rest of our lineup. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** offers the highest upside among our middle infield options with a 59.35 score. While he faces a challenging arm in Chase Burns (xERA 3.01), the combination of a strong batting order slot (#2) and a 14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage creates a high-leverage opportunity for him to contribute across our target categories.\n\nWhile the lineup is bolstered by favorable park factors and wind patterns\u2014most notably aiding **Nasim Nunez**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Brady House** against Burns\u2014we are navigating significant risk elsewhere. **Dominic Smith** is our most marginal start (41.51), barely clearing the efficiency floor due to a poor order position and a tough matchup against Ben Brown. He narrowly edged out our other reserves, but his inclusion is primarily a function of limited depth today. We are monitoring **Andy Pages** (58.80) and **Heliot Ramos** (43.69) closely, as their scores are heavily dependent on confirmed lineup slots; should **Andy Pages** slip from the #4 spot, his efficiency will crater against a disciplined opposing battery.\n\nManaging our game caps remains a priority, especially with stars like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** idle today. Among those available, **Heliot Ramos** sits near the bottom of our start threshold; he remains in the lineup only because of his projected #3 spot. We continue to hold **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, while the bench remains populated by players like **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, and 